        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nThis jacket is an example of formal daywear worn by wealthy Englishwomen in the early 17th century. The embroidery is based on designs from pattern books, herbals and emblem books. It is of a very high quality and probably professional work. Although this one was luxurious, a jacket of this type would not have been the most formal or expensive garment in Margaret Laton's wardrobe. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e48db3d1-1271-332f-82bf-37462f9ff910> .

